<title>USA: J&amp;J comfortable with Q1 estimates.</title>
<headline>J&amp;J comfortable with Q1 estimates.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Johnson &amp; Johnson said it is comfortable with analysts' first quarter earnings estimates.</p>
<p>In response to a question about a report Wednesday that the company warned analysts that first quarter results could be hurt by currency, a spokesman said, &quot;We still don't expect any problems with our ability to meet analysts' expectations.&quot;</p>
<p>According to First Call, the consensus earnings estimate for J&amp;J is $0.68 a share for the first quarter, compared to $0.59 a share the previous first quarter.</p>
<p>The stock closed down 3/8 at 57-3/8.</p>
</text>
